From 82d672507192d2fc858a9c31a40b086ec4a08ed2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: startergo <7897244+startergo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 20:25:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 39/41] [sl-port-610] Vendor woff2 + brotli decode source to
 enable WOFF2 web fonts on 10.6.

WebKit's CachedFont path skips WOFF/WOFF2 to SFNT decode on Cocoa (guarded by if not PLATFORM COCOA), assuming the platform CoreText decodes WOFF natively. 10.6 CoreText does not, and the leopard_compat CTFontManagerCreateFontDescriptorsFromData shim received raw wOF2 bytes that CGFontCreateWithDataProvider rejects (returns NULL) so all WOFF2 web fonts failed to load. USE(WOFF2) was off and no woff2/brotli ThirdParty source was present in the 610 tree (only a vestigial include path).

This vendors the woff2 + brotli (decode-only) source from the 604 tree (source/webkit/Source/ThirdParty). The older 604 woff2 layout exposes the simple buffer API in src/woff2_dec.h: ComputeWOFF2FinalSize plus ConvertWOFF2ToTTF(result,len,data,len). brotli is the flat dec/ layout (decode/state/huffman/bit_reader/dictionary). wk_woff2_wrap.cc exposes C-linkage WK_woff2_ComputeFinalSize / WK_woff2_ConvertToTTF for the Obj-C++ shim to call.

The leopard_compat shim (overlay) now detects the wOF2 magic, decodes to SFNT via these wrappers, then feeds real SFNT to CGFontCreateWithDataProvider. build_610.sh phase 3 compiles the 14 decode objects + wrapper for x86_64-10.6; phase 4 force-links them alongside leopard_compat.o.

Result: BBC Reith and other WOFF2 web fonts go from 10 error / 0 loaded to 0 error / fonts loaded.
